page('2. Dataset and visual taxonomy',P('The complete study contains 3,780 RGB renders, 540 per class. Every material contributes 30 views. The original images are 512 x 512 pixels; the evaluated holdout uses the same image dimensions. Models apply their own recorded resize, crop and normalization.'),T(counts,'Counts from frozen manifests and the validated combined-study package.'),F(gallery_path,'One actual holdout image per class, chosen by sorted path before considering prediction correctness. This descriptive gallery is not a random sample; exact IDs and image hashes are in gallery_selection.json.'),P('Ceramic in the historical corpus includes mosaic and terrazzo-like assets; concrete includes plaster and painted-wall appearances. The fresh collection uses restricted ceramic/concrete definitions. These labels are appearance categories, not laboratory measurements of composition. Coatings, rust and suede-like appearances can blur category boundaries.'))

page('3. Source audit and independence',P('All 316 original local source maps were verified against official provider records: 315 manifest-referenced maps plus one additional displacement map. The fresh collection adds 63 verified maps. Poly Haven verification compares official metadata MD5 and file size with local files, with local SHA-256 pinning; ambientCG verification compares SHA-256 and size against official archive members. These are different verification mechanisms and are not represented as remote SHA-256 matches in every case.'),
 P('Provider assets are CC0 [6,7]. The project authors the rendered images and experimental code; it does not claim authorship of third-party texture maps. Individual attribution and provider URLs remain in the source registries. License verification establishes source permissions within that evidence scope; it does not prove independent physical ancestry.'),
 P('The original registry merges known leather-generator families and a conservative wood relationship, yielding 101 groups from 105 IDs. Fresh selection checks original IDs, aliases, normalized-name families, procedural ancestry, official recipe/map identities and exact raw map reuse. No known overlap remains between development and holdout. Undisclosed captures, crops or recolours may still share physical ancestry.'),
 H('Rendering and domain differences'),P('Blender EEVEE renders a textured sphere with controlled camera, light and ground. A seven-image old-training pilot checked the fresh Blender 5.1.1 setup before bulk rendering. Framing and placement matched visually, but ground shadows were softer. The historical engine version was not fully recorded, so engine equivalence is not claimed. Restricted class semantics and rendering changes jointly limit direct transport of development estimates.'),
 H('Local study package'),P('The validated audit ZIP contains all 3,780 images and compact provenance records. Private Windows paths embedded in PNG metadata were removed from package copies while decoded pixels were verified identical. Package byte hashes therefore differ from canonical source byte hashes; both are retained. Raw textures, scene binaries and model weights are excluded. The rendered-dataset license remains unset, release approval is false and nothing has been uploaded. Appendix A identifies the archive.'))

page('4. Fixed protocol and amendments',P('All 3,150 original images are development data in V3. Historical train, validation and test directories remain lineage records; the old test had already been consulted. Known relatives crossing those old partitions are grouped together for V3. None of the original images is relabelled as a new untouched test.'),
 P('The frozen experiment uses five class-stratified outer source-group folds and three grouped inner folds, seed 20261027. Every image follows its source group. Inner selection maximizes mean Macro F1 across five declared representations and C in {0.01, 0.1, 1, 10}. Ties use declaration order, then ascending C. Scaling and fitting occur inside each training partition; outer labels never choose the representation or regularization.'),
 P('The matched ConvNeXt control selects C independently on the same partitions. ResNet-50 was declared before V3 scores and uses a fixed ten-epoch schedule on those identical outer folds, without outer-validation checkpoint selection. The initial frozen result was 79.40%, below the point target.'),
 P('After that initial result, a bounded exploratory DINOv2 follow-up compared two learning rates across the same three all-development selection folds. Its development score is explicitly adaptive and is not a replacement nested estimate. The original experiment is preserved.'),
 P('The final primary choice used development Macro F1: 0.8035245993 for frozen fusion versus 0.7724822183 for fine-tuned DINOv2. All final checkpoints were locked at 09:51:05 UTC on 27 October 2026, before first fresh prediction at 09:54:06 UTC. The four fixed models each received one clean evaluation. No fresh ranking changed model choice.'),
 P('Primary corruption tests were predeclared. The identical five corruptions were later applied to fine-tuned DINOv2 after clean scores and primary corruption outcomes had been observed. A recorded amendment labels this additional robustness comparison post hoc and exploratory. No model or clean prediction changed.'),
 H('Uncertainty'),P('Accuracy and Macro F1 are image-weighted. Confidence intervals use 10,000 class-stratified source-group cluster bootstrap draws, seed 62642, with percentile 95% limits. Each sampled group brings all its images with multiplicity. Paired differences use matching images and source draws. Intervals condition on saved predictions; they do not include refitting, selection uncertainty or dependent cross-validation training sets. Only three new groups per class constrain uncertainty resolution.'))

pipelines=table('pipelines',['Pipeline','Representation / input','Adaptation and budget'],[['Primary frozen fusion','DINOv2 small with registers, 224 + 336; ConvNeXt-Tiny, 224','3,072 features; scaled balanced logistic head; inner C selection'],['ConvNeXt control','Pooled ConvNeXt-Tiny, 224','Frozen backbone; independently selected logistic C'],['Fixed ResNet-50','ImageNet-1K V2 weights, 224','Two head-only epochs, then layer4 + head; ten fixed epochs'],['Fine-tuned DINOv2','Small with registers; CLS + patch mean, 336','Two head-only epochs, then last two blocks; six development fits, five-epoch final fit']])
page('5. Pipelines and compute-budget confounds',T(pipelines,'Model definitions from frozen configurations and checkpoint metadata. Exact weight identities are in the evidence bundle.'),P('The primary vector concatenates CLS, patch mean and patch population standard deviation for DINOv2 at 224 and 336 pixels, then adds pooled ConvNeXt features. Registers are not patches. StandardScaler and a class-balanced L2 logistic regression head use lbfgs, tolerance 0.0001 and up to 3,000 iterations. A convergence warning fails the run rather than silently changing the solver.'),P('Frozen feature extraction is deterministic and learns no dataset-specific representation. Cached features can be shared across grouped folds, while the scaler and classifier must be refitted within each training fold. The canonical caches and final frozen run exactly reproduce the earlier feature arrays and OOF prediction files.'),P('ResNet uses AdamW, head learning rate 0.0003 and layer4 learning rate 0.00001, weight decay 0.01, label smoothing 0.05 and a fixed cosine schedule. Batch-normalization running statistics stay frozen. Its ten-epoch final fit uses all development images and does not consult fresh labels.'),P('DINOv2 adaptation searches backbone learning rates 3e-6 and 1e-5 with a maximum of ten epochs and development patience three. Best epochs at 1e-5 are 6, 5 and 3; their rounded median yields five epochs for the all-development fit. This stage follows the initial result and must retain its exploratory label.'),P('The pipelines differ in pretraining corpora and objectives, input resolution, feature dimension, number of backbone passes, search budget and amount of adaptation. Their measured differences compare complete workflows. They cannot isolate a transformer-versus-CNN effect, the benefit of self-supervision alone or equal-compute efficiency. No audit establishes the absence of public texture overlap in backbone pretraining data.'))

