page('16. Limitations, conclusion and next steps',H('What the evidence supports'),P('The preselected primary achieved the requested 80% point target on a clean, independently collected source holdout. This is a completed measured result: 80.16% accuracy and Macro F1 0.7952. The highest observed comparison is fine-tuned DINOv2 at 86.83%, but paired uncertainty does not establish its superiority and its exploratory status remains unchanged.'),H('What remains unresolved'),P('Only three new families per class constrain inference. Thirty views per material are dependent, known-family grouping is conservative and physical ancestry is incomplete. Public texture overlap with backbone pretraining data has not been audited. Restricted class semantics and Blender-version differences complicate transfer from the original corpus. No real-world validation exists.'),P('Compression is a major practical limitation. The primary misses the target on low brightness, blur, JPEG compression and reduced resolution. Per-class performance is uneven, with ceramic, concrete, stone and leather exposing boundary problems. Perfect sampled recall for some classes is not a population guarantee. Calibration and abstention diagnostics are descriptive and do not validate an operating threshold.'),P('Model comparisons confound architecture, pretraining, resolution, adaptation and compute budgets. The bounded DINOv2 follow-up was motivated by the initial outcome; later robustness was post hoc. The historical test was previously consulted. All these decisions are disclosed rather than presented as one fully preregistered experiment.'),H('Recommended next experiment'),P('Freeze a new evaluation plan before gathering or scoring additional sources. Priorities are more independently verified families in ambiguous categories, held-out scenes and genuine photographs, stronger compression coverage and development-only threshold calibration. Budget-matched ablations would better separate representation effects from extra passes or adaptation. Any subsequent tuning on this now-scored holdout requires a new independent assessment.'),P('The final artifacts support research, teaching and inspection of comparable synthetic renders. They do not identify physical composition or justify safety-critical material decisions. Dataset publication remains a separate owner decision; the complete audit package is prepared locally with no upload.'))

