page('Appendix C. Scalar metrics and interpretation',T(mt,'Primary clean holdout. Scores are fractions except dimensionless loss metrics; all intervals use the recorded fixed-prediction source-group bootstrap.'),P('Accuracy is correct predictions divided by images. Macro precision, recall and F1 average over the seven fixed classes. Weighted F1 uses class support; on this balanced holdout it equals Macro F1. Brier score is the mean summed squared class-probability error; log loss clips probabilities according to evaluator conventions. ECE aggregates absolute confidence/accuracy gaps across 15 equal-width bins.'),P('Each source contributes exactly 30 images on the fresh endpoint, so image-weighted and source-balanced accuracy coincide numerically. Source-balanced accuracy is an average of within-source accuracies, not multiview voting. Group-level mean-probability predictions are separate secondary diagnostics and must not replace the primary image endpoint.'),P('These pooled scalar intervals are not per-class confidence intervals. Per-class support and point metrics are shown in Section 10 and the saved evaluator outputs. Only three source groups per class limit class-level precision; no additional interval has been estimated during report production.'),P('The bound at 80% is an engineering point target, not a hypothesis-test threshold or a guaranteed lower confidence limit. Retaining all outcomes, explicit population definitions and source hashes is essential to interpreting the result.'))

